# rm326, the forgiving tally (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm326
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rmx_lionel_platt
written_by codex
title the forgiving tally
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=woodcutter
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk cuts_a_second_notch_when_a_debt_is_forgiven
likes fried_fish singing tidy_house thunder
dislikes crowds flies
fears a_kindness_counted_as_profit an_unclaimed_envelope
hopes a_clear_shelf_at_home a_tally_that_matches_both_ends
topics work +0.6 friends +0.3 food +0.3 weather +0.4 dreams +0.3
styles comfort=generous gossip=discreet refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# pares a second notch across each forgiven debt, carries a letter kept for a stubbornly absent recipient and has a steady voice for singing over bad weather.

words
oath! = Split my last lath | Warp the tally
saying! = Cut across a debt to clear it | Kindness keeps its own account
tally = my slender tally | the little squared stick
cross = the second notch | a crosswise nick
fold = the letter fold | my undelivered packet
fish = the hot brown fillet | a crisp fish corner
rack = a row of square hooks | the neatly spaced pegs
buzz = an unwelcome fly | the hovering pest
roar = the long thunder roll | a deep booming note
scrap = a curl of soft wood | the pale clean shaving
ruler = a straight measuring slip | my marked wooden foot
grain = the true grain | a pale line in the board
curl = the splintered end | a standing sliver
drybit = the sheltered patch | a dry corner of the stack
part = the lower harmony | my steady low part
board = a planed offcut | the smooth square
seat = a modest stool | my little wooden seat
coin = the last small copper | a spare bit of copper
wrap = a greaseproof fold | the second twist of paper

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : A full account can be kept in a book. The Bright One also sees what I choose to let go uncollected.
opinion @2 dole for 2 : A fellow wolf's supper shouldn't go to bed itself just because the buyer has an empty pocket.
opinion @3 merchants for 1 : Somebody has to pay for timber before a customer ever gets to look at the grain.
opinion @4 newcomers for 1 : Offer a newcomer an unoccupied piece of board. Everybody has to take a first hold somewhere.
opinion @5 road against 1 : A late wagon can cost a whole afternoon without putting a scratch on a single piece of freight.
opinion @6 watch for 1 : I'll give credit for a quiet counter to the feet that walk the night round.
opinion @7 drink against 1 : A cup that eats the money for a family's cupboard has taken an excessive helping.
opinion @8 city for 1 : A wolf can come through the Commons with sawdust under the cuffs and have something to offer the next street.
opinion @9 strangers for 1 : We haven't done business yet. That's an opening, not an argument for shutting the door.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Here's a clear end of timber for your parcel. Welcome. | Come within reach of the clean board.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : First light sits kindly on the grain today. | Morning, with a fresh tally still to fill.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Dry off where the pine smells strongest. | Welcome beneath this bit of sound timber.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : Stay on the planed side and come close. | Here's an eye and an ear clear of the work.
line @5 greet.return : A welcome with both ends of it accounted for. | Glad of the good sound your greeting makes.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Some voices live on my credit side for good. | Here's some room cleared with you in mind.
line @7 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : The day's nearly squared away. A word's welcome. | We've enough light left for kind faces.
line @8 farewell : May your load lie true through all the turnings. | Home safe with the weight settled evenly.
line @9 farewell.return : I'll keep our account in friendly order. | A peaceful road beyond this parting place.
line @10 again.open : Another turn across the marked board. | Here's that voice again, right on the grain.
line @11 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : No tally needed on a place held for family. | Set your knees under this side beside me.
line @12 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here with the fine sawdust! | A good corner left free for you!
line @13 react.news : Let's have the account with the weight on both ends. | Where did that word first take hold, I wonder.
line @14 react.news.new : There's a mark my tally didn't have before. | First sight of that particular turn in the grain.
line @15 react.news.known : I've an older nick for the same account. | The first telling had about that weight too.
line @16 react.news.doubt : I can't make the two notches match on that statement. | Something rough has slipped in beneath a very smooth telling.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Let the account wait. The hurt wants company. | That brings a heavy end of the timber down on a household.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : I've a good strong harmony for a word like that. | That's news to set the last notch shining.
line @19 answer.how : Good at the grain and easy at heart. | My work and my word line up well enough.
line @20 decline : I'd have to leave another wolf short to cover that promise. | There isn't enough in my reckoning to take that on honestly.
line @21 accept_decline : A straight answer leaves both ends sound. | The limit you set is fair enough for me.
line @22 sympathise : Come sit. Nobody has to lift the whole board alone. | The load can lie still while you find your breath.
line @23 thank : I have an excellent memory for that sort of kindness. | That deserves a deep and favourable notch.
line @24 deflect_thanks : A gift goes across my stick with the account already cleared. | Just take the comfort without carrying a debt.
line @25 preclose : I've a few small nicks to put in order. | Time I went back to my stubborn little errand.
line @26 accept_preclose : Keep your day's balance as even as you can. | Go on. I can hold this end awhile.
line @27 farewell [here.weather=rain] : Stay well inside the drips at the roof edge. | Wrap the good paper with the folds downhill.
line @28 farewell [here.time=night] : May the hearth be bright when you get there. | A gentle hour when your latch drops.
line @29 greet [pair.band=friends] : There's the voice that can hold up my lower part. | Room at the song and at the board.
line @30 preclose [self.working=yes] : The stack has stood without my eye long enough. | I'll settle the timber before I settle myself.
line @31 answer.how [here.time=night] : Almost ready for a clear table and a quiet voice. | Worn just enough to take a decent rest.
scene crossnick
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut #cross# where a wolf need never pay me back. | A single mark is a debt. Overcut it once and the stick has a kinder memory.
b : Why keep the mark if the debt is gone? | Does the wood know the difference?
a : Lest a busy head send a fresh bill for an old kindness. | My thumb does. It keeps me from asking twice.

scene shelftidy
when topic=pastimes self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave one peg on #rack# bare. | An empty space on my shelf has a proper occupation.
b : Waiting for another hat? | Serving as furniture for a pocket of air?
a : For whatever a guest comes carrying. A well-appointed house can take a surprise. | For a little while. Then a late parcel generally asks to borrow it.

scene fried
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take #fish# and I'll fold #wrap# round the rest. | I can offer you a browned edge of fish before it cools.
b : I'll take the bit nearest your thumb. | I'd rather not take your best bit.
a : Good. It's crisp right through and the wrapping won't stick. | I've saved a fine one under the fold. Eat before the steam spoils the edge.

scene sing
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take #part# when two voices start up close together. | A low note can prop up a hesitant voice without taking the tune.
b : Do you have to know the words? | Wouldn't it be simpler just to sing louder?
a : Only where to breathe. The words come clear when the rest are comfortable. | Lift underneath and the other voice can stay where it's happy.

scene thunder
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #roar# puts a fine bass under anything a wolf wants to sing. | I enjoy the little trail of silence behind a thunderclap.
b : There's not much use in trying to outsing it. | You mean after the shaking stops?
a : No need. I enjoy keeping time with a voice much grander than mine. | Just before. You feel the board tremble after the sound starts to leave.

scene fly
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #buzz# has an absurd affection for the crispest flank of my fish. | A fly can't read the courteous distance I've left between plates.
b : Cover it with the paper, then. | What would make the distance legible?
a : I have. Now the pest's trying to inspect the underside. | A generous sweep of cloth. I can make my meaning quite clear.

scene crowd
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What's a kind way through a crowd when both elbows are carrying planks? | How would you give a little breathing room without shouting?
b : Wait for a turn and call out which end is coming. | Raise your free hand before you lift the wood.
a : Agreed. Hearing the purpose often makes a decent space. | A moment well spent to preserve everybody's ribs and good will.

scene keeper
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.job=woodcutter self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I turn #grain# toward the buyer before entering a price. | Every board at #self.workplace# has a second side deserving a look.
b : Even if it shows a rough spot? | Is a pretty surface misleading?
a : Especially so. I'd rather explain a knot than have a neighbour find it under strain. | Only half a promise. I sell the whole thickness.

scene familyseat
when topic=family self.spouse
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd build #seat# even and broad for #self.spouse#. | I have a quiet note of thanks to take home to #self.spouse#.
b : Where would the stool stand? | What would you set the words to?
a : Near enough to the table for our knees to touch underneath. | No tune. There's speech that deserves to keep its ordinary pitch.

scene hand
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.hand
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd value a second eye on my figures from #self.hand#. | I've a troublesome plank I'd save to discuss with #self.hand#.
b : What made you look again? | Would you own a mistake to a worker?
a : Two ends with the same mark but different wear. I keep a ruler handy. | Yes. Errors multiply wonderfully in the dark.

scene devout
when topic=dreams self.piety=devout
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I'd like the Bright One to find the grain of my word running true at day's end. | My wish is to remember the debts I owe more readily than those due me.
b : Even when you'll lose by it? | Can one prayer alter a memory?
a : It isn't always losing. A cleared debt makes a neighbour easier in the street. | It can give the next notch a purpose before I carve.

scene owners
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's always a little weight of somebody else's money on the counter I keep. | I account for the last shaving even when I'd like to call it a gift.
b : What do you get to give freely then? | Do you remember it all?
a : My own share. It's worth keeping very clear which hand is being generous. | I keep #tally# with me. Pride isn't as fit for carrying figures.

scene letterdoor
when topic=dreams
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I'm still carrying #fold# that ought to be under a grand roof already. | A good seal grows worn while its intended owner stays elsewhere.
b : Couldn't you set it down outside the door? | Does a worn seal trouble you?
a : A sill won't give its word it has the letter. I'd be uneasy all night. | It does. I haven't the right to improve it and won't let it come apart through carelessness.

scene office
when topic=land self.quarter=office
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Here in the Office quarter there's paper for reckoning exactly how much sawdust sticks to my cuffs. | Clean faces on figures please me as well as clean faces on cut grain.
b : Do you enter the sawdust as profit? | Is that an Office habit you take home?
a : Only if somebody offers me a handsome price to take the lot away. | Yes. It doesn't disturb a quiet home to know exactly what the cupboard holds.

scene towntrade
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The Commons will teach a trader to make enough room at the board for somebody carrying dinner. | In Ridgemere a long plank needs three voices to get round a street turn.
b : How much room's a decent amount? | I can only think of the two ends. Who's the third?
a : Enough to set a small hot parcel down without the buyer having to step back out in the crowd. | The wolf already round the turn who calls the path clear.

scene earnprice
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A cheap wrong board can cost two fine ones before the job is complete. | If a price buys the right measure I can defend it in a neighbour's kitchen.
b : You'd still like to sell the dearer one. | Your buyer may only have the cheap price to hand.
a : I would like a second visit when the work's stood a winter. | Then let's see if a smaller sound piece will do the job.

scene donate
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does offer / accept / assess
a : Let me put the cost of another bowl among my own tally notches. | I've saved something for a hand that's come up short this week.
b : I'd receive it more easily if I needn't hear my name read out. | I'd put it back when I can manage.
a : Your name needn't come anywhere near my pencil. | Give when you can and keep no particular wolf in arrears.

scene wagons
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A late wagon can put an entire row of sound timber out of use for the morning. | We can have a whole task laid straight except the load that hasn't got here.
b : You can put the time to another job? | Is it worth shaving the minor bits first?
a : I can if the delay's admitted early. An honest word saves an idle hour. | Quite. Sometimes the smallest scraps take the longest to settle just right.

scene wrapside
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The clean fold round a fish supper keeps the crispness in the right place. | I keep the fish lifted above the grease while I walk.
b : Where exactly's the right place? | In what sort of delicate contrivance?
a : At the browned edges. Let the steam go out above the middle. | Two plain scraps laid across the folded paper. Enough to keep dinner from taking a long bath.

scene roarcount
when topic=weather world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can sing through the minute before thunder starts without a single thought of money. | Thunder's best roll comes free in a poor week.
b : What happens to the figures while you're singing? | But suppose your roof still leaks?
a : They can wait for the silence. Debts aren't in fear of being forgotten. | Put the basin where the drops have good rhythm. Then see about a patch.

scene squarecase
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like to put #ruler# beside a deliberately crooked piece. | A wood curl held up to the light can tell you why a cut went wrong.
b : Wouldn't a straight piece be better company? | And is it all the fault of the blade?
a : I learn more from the disagreement. A straight piece stays useful either way. | No. I sometimes insisted on going against #grain# to save myself an extra minute.

scene truewage
when topic=work
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A wolf paid for a whole board should get the sound edge as well as the heart. | I'd have the time spent straightening a load counted in its price.
b : Surely the outer scraps go to the keeper? | Wouldn't that make everything dearer?
a : The buyer should know if the deal includes the right to keep the cuttings. | Only clear. A hidden charge still comes out of somebody's supper.

scene welcome
when topic=newcomer
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take #drybit# while I shift the loose timber. | A new face can have the first look along the true edge here.
b : I'll tuck my bundle close. | I'd hardly know what I was looking for.
a : Thank you. We like a welcome to leave enough room to work as well. | Look for light under the ruler. The timber will explain the rest.

scene mirror
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old story follows a tally cut so lightly only its maker could read it. | I know a tale where a single shaving pays a huge board debt.
b : How was anybody to know when it was cleared? | What makes the shaving so precious?
a : By the second cut. That one was deep enough for all the street to see. | It was the piece that raised a table leg where a whole meal would have slid off.

scene quietdoor
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd deliver one special envelope and go home with my pocket lying quite flat. | Some sorts of debt had better go to the exact address in a single piece.
b : You wouldn't mind the pocket feeling strange? | A gift can come to a different door and still be welcome.
a : I'd mark the emptiness with #scrap# if I felt lopsided. | True. A sealed word is less readily transferred than a gift of bread.

scene household
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a clean hour away from trade to share with #self.spouse#. | I would leave a good end of fish on the warm plate for #self.spouse#.
b : Is a whole hour without an account in it possible? | Would you keep count of which part was yours?
a : In a home with two chairs prepared, a decent hour is quite a small demand. | No. Supper's a pleasure, not a sale.

scene singalong
when topic=pastimes
does tease / tease.return / laugh
a : That note's sitting down on the job; shall I prop it up? | Your song has a very honest way of arriving late.
b : If you'll saw it exactly to size. | I was letting your harmony get a lead on me.
a : Then I'd have to go round charging by the foot of chorus. | A generous explanation. Come in on the next clap with me.

scene letterrain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : This coat must not leak at the corner with #fold# in it. | I don't much mind wet shoulders if my papers stay crisp.
b : Turn your body with the wet side to the wind. | They're wrapped twice, aren't they?
a : That's the stance. The rest of me will dry quite readily. | One fold for the letter and another so I don't mistake my own writing for the address.

scene handmeasure
when topic=work
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : How would you finish this straight edge with its sharp standing sliver? | Would you price a pretty offcut before feeling whether it's firm?
b : A single light pass along the splinter first. | Press its end against a sound board and listen.
a : Yes. The tool should leave #curl# no chance at a worker's cuff. | Good. A solid edge and a pretty face might earn different prices.

scene lasting
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd like the largest mark on my last tally to be a debt I chose to forgive. | Some evenings I can see every generous piece of work in the order of my shelves.
b : A whole lost sum worth a place of honour? | What does generosity look like on a shelf?
a : A fair trade: the worry off another household for a harmless cut in wood. | A well-fitted open space for something that's gone where it was needed.

story two_edges [topic=work]
  : I cut a tally for a borrowed plank. When I went to settle it I found the nick on both edges of the stick.
  : There had only been one loan. I thought back until I remembered making the second cut to test a new knife.
  b : How did you distinguish them?
  : The test nick slanted with the grain. A real charge ran across it. I've kept careless cutting away from my accounts since.

story fish_balance [topic=food]
  : Two crisp fish ends in a folded paper looked equal. I gave one a lift and felt it weigh almost nothing.
  : It was only skin formed over a pocket of steam. The other had the supper in it.
  b : Which did you take?
  : Shared the proper end and divided the crackling skin. Both of us had what we'd thought was on the paper.

story wet_door [topic=lore]
  : A traveller in a story carried a letter through a week of downpours. Took off a coat, then a waistcoat, to keep the folded pages dry.
  : The door opened on a thoroughly soaked wolf and one immaculate seal.
  b : Did the letter explain the soaking?
  : The first line sent good wishes for kindly weather. One can't shift a word once the seal is set.

story low_voice [topic=pastimes]
  : I was singing a slow part over a board when a low growl went on beneath the note after I stopped. I tried the note again to see what answered.
  : The window rattled and the light slipped sideways over the grain.
  b : Thunder in the hills?
  : A cart making the turn outside. I gave it a decent last note and went back to work.

story clean_space [topic=dreams]
  : I cleared the top shelf and set my prayer book in the centre. There was a pale rectangle at each side where a box had stood.
  : I started putting the boxes back, saw how square the pale spaces looked, and left them alone.
  b : What occupies those spaces now?
  : Sometimes bread for a neighbour. Sometimes just air. Both have good cause to be there.

rule @stack
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=woodcutter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Line up the lower edge first. | Good clear grain to the light.

rule @letter
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Paper dry at the inner fold. | A coat can stand the wetter side.

rule @prayer
when concept=bark self.piety=devout
does aside
cooldown 8h
say May the Bright One see level grain in this gift. | Let the unasked kindness come to mind.

rule @tally
when concept=bark self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mark the bit that went freely. | A small account can deserve a good line.

rule @home
when concept=bark self.married=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two clean seats for the evening. | The unpriced part of a day.

rule @fish
when concept=bark self.likes=fried_fish
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Still crisp along the lean edge. | Share while the steam's rising.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : I'll make some room along the counter for a new voice.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, no need to measure out your welcome again.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The work has gone quieter. I'll gladly give you a full hearing.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Bring your errand forward and leave your anger a pace behind.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.role=merchant self.job=woodcutter self.workplace] : I run #self.workplace#. What goes out under my word has had its edges checked.
dlg @6 resident.job : I square the patch of board where somebody else will begin.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : This much has reached my working board. #world.news#
dlg @8 resident.bye : Leave our account easy on your shoulders.
dlg @9 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : You're welcome to examine the measure before we consider the price.
dlg @10 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Bare shelves for the moment. I'll listen to offers from a seller.
dlg @11 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : Mm. The tally's shut and my eyes have followed.
dlg @12 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a clear grain and a clear welcome to you.
dlg @13 shop.prices : You'll see the figure beside the goods. Ask me what needful work it covers. #shop_offer#
dlg @14 shop.bye : Thank you for the time you've spent examining my work.
dlg @15 resident.hub [here.weather=rain] : Even a wet visit can come in and lay its bundle down.
graft resident.hub
choice What does the crossed cut stand for? -> cleared_debt
node cleared_debt
say A single stroke keeps a thing due in mind. A crosswise cut tells my thumb I've already chosen to give the thing freely.
choice Why leave it where you can feel it? -> fair_memory
choice Close the tally awhile. -> hub
node fair_memory
say So some future tight week doesn't make me remember the owing and forget the giving. The gift would hardly be worth the name.
choice That squares the account. -> hub
choice Good will between us. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice May I inspect the underside? [here.shop=open] -> underside_view
node underside_view
say Of course. Let me show how much sound material your money would purchase, all the way through. Turn the edge toward this patch of light.
choice What about the little nick? -> edge_nick
choice Let's look at the rest. -> greet
node edge_nick
say I'd mark it on the record of the sale and tell you how much trim you'll need. No fair measure leaves a buyer guessing where the grain ends.
choice Let me consider the goods. -> greet
choice My thanks for the look. -> bye
